          %h2#idea Idea
          %p
            There may be different
            = succeed "-" do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/model+category"} model category
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/mathematical+structure"} structures
            on the
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/category"} category
            of
            = succeed "." do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/diffeological+spaces"} diffeological spaces
          %p
            Of practical interest would be a model structure whose
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/weak+equivalences"} weak equivalences
            are the
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/isomorphisms"} isomorphisms
            on standard
            %em smooth
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/homotopy+groups"} homotopy groups
            of
            = succeed "," do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/diffeological+spaces"} diffeological spaces
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/weak+equivalences"} weak equivalences
            between the
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/cohesive+shapes"} cohesive shapes
            of
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/diffeological+spaces"} diffeological spaces
            regarded as the
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/concrete+objects"} concrete objects
            in the
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/cohesive+%28%E2%88%9E%2C1%29-topos"} cohesive (∞,1)-topos
            of
            = succeed "." do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/smooth+%E2%88%9E-groupoids"} smooth ∞-groupoids
            %em
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/shape+via+cohesive+path+%E2%88%9E-groupoid"} shape via cohesive path ∞-groupoid
            these are detected by smooth functions out of
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/simplices"} simplices
            or
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/cubes"} cubes
            with their canonical diffeological structure (as discussed in
            = succeed ")." do
              %a{:href => "#ChristensenWu14"} Christensen-Wu 14
          %p
            A model category with this property has been claimed in
            = succeed ",," do
              %a{:href => "#HaraguchiShimakawa13"} Haraguchi-Shimakawa 13
            %a{:href => "#HaraguchiShimakawa20"} Haraguchi-Shimakawa 20
          %p
            Another model category structure is discussed in
            = succeed "," do
              %a{:href => "#Kihara16"} Kihara 16
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/singular+simplicial+complexes"} singular simplicial complexes
            are
            = succeed ")." do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/fibrant+objects"} fibrant objects
          %h2#details Details
          %p
            The approach of
            = succeed "," do
              %a{:href => "#HaraguchiShimakawa13"} Haraguchi-Shimakawa 13
            %a{:href => "#HaraguchiShimakawa20"} Haraguchi-Shimakawa 20
            proceeds as follows:
          %div
            #AdjunctionBetweenTopologicalSpacesAndDiffeologicalSpaces.num_prop
              %h6#proposition Proposition
              %p
                %strong
                  (
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/adjunction+between+topological+spaces+and+diffeological+spaces"}> adjunction between topological spaces and diffeological spaces
                  )
              %p
                There is a pair of
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/adjoint+functors"} adjoint functors
              #eq:AdjointFunctorsBetweenTopSpAndDifflgSp.maruku-equation
                %span.maruku-eq-number (1)
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi TopSp
                      %munderover
                        %mrow
                          %mphantom
                            %mi AA
                          %mo ⊥
                          %mphantom
                            %mi AA
                        %munder
                          %mo ⟶
                          %mi Cdfflg
                        %mover
                          %mo ⟵
                          %mi Dtplg
                      %mi DifflgSp
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                      TopSp
                      \\underoverset{
                      \\underset{
                      Cdfflg
                      }{\longrightarrow}
                      }{
                      \\overset{
                      Dtplg
                      }{\longleftarrow}
                      }{\phantom{AA}\bot\phantom{AA}}
                      DifflgSp
              %p
                between the
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/categories"} categories
                of
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Top"} TopologicalSpaces
                and of
                = succeed "," do
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/DiffeologicalSpaces"} DiffeologicalSpaces
              %ul
                %li
                  %p
                    %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                      %semantics
                        %mrow
                          %mi Cdfflg
                        %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} Cdfflg
                    takes a
                    %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/topological+space"} topological space
                    %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                      %semantics
                        %mrow
                          %mi X
                        %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} X
                    to the
                    = succeed "," do
                      %strong continuous diffeology
                    %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                      %semantics
                        %mrow
                          %msub
                            %mi X
                            %mi s
                        %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} X_s
                    whose plots
                    %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                      %semantics
                        %mrow
                          %msub
                            %mi U
                            %mi s
                          %mo →
                          %msub
                            %mi X
                            %mi s
                        %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} U_s \to X_s
                    are the
                    %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/continuous+functions"} continuous functions
                    (from the underlying
                    %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/topological+space"} topological space
                    of the
                    %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/domain"} domain
                    = succeed ")." do
                      %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                        %semantics
                          %mrow
                            %mi U
                          %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} U
                %li
                  %p
                    %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                      %semantics
                        %mrow
                          %mi Dtplg
                        %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} Dtplg
                    takes a
                    %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/diffeological+space"} diffeological space
                    to the
                    %strong diffeological topology
                    (
                    %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/D-topology"}> D-topology
                    ), namely the
                    %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/topological+space"} topological space
                    with the same underlying set
                    %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                      %semantics
                        %mrow
                          %msub
                            %mi X
                            %mi s
                        %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} X_s
                    and with the
                    %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/final+topology"} final topology
                    that makes all its plots
                    %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                      %semantics
                        %mrow
                          %msub
                            %mi U
                            %mi s
                          %mo →
                          %msub
                            %mi X
                            %mi s
                        %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} U_{s} \to X_{s}
                    into
                    = succeed ":" do
                      %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/continuous+functions"} continuous functions
                    = succeed "." do
                      %em
                        %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/D-topology"} D-topology
                  %p
                    Hence a
                    %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/subset"} subset
                    %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                      %semantics
                        %mrow
                          %mi O
                          %mo ⊂
                          %mo ♭
                          %mi X
                        %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} O \subset \flat X
                    is an
                    %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/open+subset"} open subset
                    in the
                    %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/D-topology"} D-topology
                    precisely if for each plot
                    %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                      %semantics
                        %mrow
                          %mi f
                          %mo{:lspace => "verythinmathspace"} :
                          %mi U
                          %mo →
                          %mi X
                        %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} f \colon U \to X
                    the
                    %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/preimage"} preimage
                    %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                      %semantics
                        %mrow
                          %msup
                            %mi f
                            %mrow
                              %mo{:lspace => "verythinmathspace", :rspace => "0em"} −
                              %mn 1
                          %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                          %mi O
                          %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                          %mo ⊂
                          %mi U
                        %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} f^{-1}(O) \subset U
                    is an
                    %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/open+subset"} open subset
                    in the
                    %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Cartesian+space"} Cartesian space
                    = succeed "." do
                      %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                        %semantics
                          %mrow
                            %mi U
                          %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} U
              %p Moreover:
              %ol
                %li
                  %p
                    the
                    %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/fixed+point+of+an+adjunction"} fixed points of this adjunction
                    %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                      %semantics
                        %mrow
                          %mi X
                          %mo ∈
                        %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} X \in
                    %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Top"} TopologicalSpaces
                    (those for which the
                    %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/counit+of+an+adjunction"} counit
                    is an
                    = succeed "," do
                      %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/isomorphism"} isomorphism
                    = succeed ")" do
                      %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/homeomorphism"} homeomorphism
                    %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Delta-generated+topological+spaces"} Delta-generated topological spaces
                    (
                    %a{:href => "Delta-generated+topological+space#AsDTopologicalSpaces"} i.e.
                    = succeed "):" do
                      %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/D-topological+spaces"} D-topological spaces
                  .maruku-equation
                    %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                      %semantics
                        %mrow
                          %mi X
                          %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                          %mspace{:width => "thinmathspace"}
                          %mtext is
                          %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                          %mi Δ
                          %mtext -generated
                          %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                          %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                          %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                          %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                          %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                          %mo ⇔
                          %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                          %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                          %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                          %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                          %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                          %mi Dtplg
                          %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                          %mi Cdfflg
                          %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                          %mi X
                          %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                          %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                          %munderover
                            %mo ⟶
                            %mo ≃
                            %mrow
                              %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                              %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                              %msub
                                %mi ϵ
                                %mi X
                              %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                              %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                          %mi X
                        %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                          X \;\,\text{is}\;\Delta\text{-generated}
                          \\;\;\;\;\;
                          \\Leftrightarrow
                          \\;\;\;\;\;
                          Dtplg(Cdfflg(X))
                          \\underoverset{\simeq}{\;\;\epsilon_X\;\;}{\longrightarrow}
                          X
                %li
                  %p
                    this is an
                    = succeed "," do
                      %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/idempotent+adjunction"} idempotent adjunction
                    = succeed "-generated/" do
                      %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                        %semantics
                          %mrow
                            %mi Δ
                          %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \Delta
                    %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/D-topological+spaces"} D-topological spaces
                    as a
                    %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/reflective+subcategory"} reflective subcategory
                    inside
                    %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/diffeological+spaces"} diffeological spaces
                    and a
                    %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/coreflective+subcategory"} coreflective subcategory
                    inside all
                    = succeed ":" do
                      %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/topological+spaces"} topological spaces
              #eq:DeltaGeneratedSpacesInIdempotentAdjunction.maruku-equation
                %span.maruku-eq-number (2)
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi TopologicalSpaces
                      %munderover
                        %mrow
                          %mphantom
                            %mi AA
                          %mo ⊥
                          %mphantom
                            %mi AA
                        %munder
                          %mo ⟶
                          %mi Cdfflg
                        %mover
                          %mo ↩
                          %mrow
                      %mi DTopologicalSpaces
                      %munderover
                        %mrow
                          %mphantom
                            %mi AA
                          %mo ⊥
                          %mphantom
                            %mi AA
                        %munder
                          %mo ↪
                          %mrow
                        %mover
                          %mo ⟵
                          %mi Dtplg
                      %mi DiffeologicalSpaces
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                      TopologicalSpaces
                      \\underoverset
                      {
                      \\underset{
                      Cdfflg
                      }{\longrightarrow}
                      }
                      {
                      \\overset{
                      }{\hookleftarrow}
                      }
                      {\phantom{AA}\bot\phantom{AA}}
                      DTopologicalSpaces
                      \\underoverset
                      {
                      \\underset{
                      }{\hookrightarrow}
                      }
                      {
                      \\overset{
                      Dtplg
                      }{\longleftarrow}
                      }
                      {\phantom{AA}\bot\phantom{AA}}
                      DiffeologicalSpaces
              %p
                Finally, these adjunctions are a sequence of
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Quillen+equivalences"} Quillen equivalences
                with respect to the:
              %table
                %thead
                  %tr
                    %th
                    %th
                    %th
                %tbody
                  %tr
                    %td{:style => "text-align: left;"}
                      %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/classical+model+structure+on+topological+spaces"} classical model structure on topological spaces
                    %td{:style => "text-align: left;"}
                      %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/model+structure+on+D-topological+spaces"} model structure on D-topological spaces
                    %td{:style => "text-align: left;"}
                      %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/model+structure+on+diffeological+spaces"} model structure on diffeological spaces
              %blockquote
                %p
                  Caution: There was a gap in the original proof that
                  = succeed "." do
                    %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                      %semantics
                        %mrow
                          %mi DTopologicalSpaces
                          %msub
                            %mo ≃
                            %mi Quillen
                          %mi DiffeologicalSpaces
                        %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} DTopologicalSpaces \simeq_{Quillen} DiffeologicalSpaces
                  = succeed "." do
                    %a{:href => "model+structure+on+diffeological+spaces#References"} here
            %p
              Essentially these adjunctions and their properties are observed in
              = succeed "," do
                %a{:href => "diffeological+space#SYH10"} Shimakawa, Yoshida &amp; Haraguchi 2010, Prop. 3.1, Prop. 3.2, Lem. 3.3
              = succeed "." do
                %a{:href => "D-topology#CSW13"} Christensen, Sinnamon &amp; Wu 2014, Sec. 3.2
              %a{:href => "#model+structure+on+Delta-generated+topological+spaces#Haraguchi13"} Haraguchi 13, Thm. 3.3
              (on the left) and
              %a{:href => "model+structure+on+diffeological+spaces#HaraguchiShimakawa13"} Haraguchi-Shimakawa 13, Sec. 7
              (on the right).
            .proof
              %h6#proof Proof
              %p
                We spell out the existence of the
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/idempotent+adjunction"} idempotent adjunction
                = succeed ":" do
                  %a.maruku-eqref{:href => "#eq:DeltaGeneratedSpacesInIdempotentAdjunction"} (2)
              %p
                First, to see we have an
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/adjunction"} adjunction
                = succeed "," do
                  %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                    %semantics
                      %mrow
                        %mi Dtplg
                        %mo ⊣
                        %mi Cdfflg
                      %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} Dtplg \dashv Cdfflg
                = succeed ")." do
                  %a{:href => "adjoint+functor#eq:HomIsomorphismForAdjointFunctors"} here
              %p
                Let
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi X
                      %mo ∈
                      %mi DiffeologicalSpaces
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} X \in DiffeologicalSpaces
                and
                = succeed "." do
                  %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                    %semantics
                      %mrow
                        %mi Y
                        %mo ∈
                        %mi TopologicalSpaces
                      %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} Y \in TopologicalSpaces
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                      %mo{:lspace => "verythinmathspace", :rspace => "0em"} −
                      %msub
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                        %mi s
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} (-)_s
                for the underlying sets. Then a
                = succeed "," do
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/morphism"} morphism
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/continuous+function"} continuous function
                of the form
              .maruku-equation
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi f
                      %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                      %mo{:lspace => "verythinmathspace"} :
                      %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                      %mi Dtplg
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                      %mi X
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                      %mo ⟶
                      %mi Y
                      %mspace{:width => "thinmathspace"}
                      %mo ,
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                      f \;\colon\; Dtplg(X) \longrightarrow Y
                      \\,,
              %p
                is a
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/function"} function
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %msub
                        %mi f
                        %mi s
                      %mo{:lspace => "verythinmathspace"} :
                      %msub
                        %mi X
                        %mi s
                      %mo →
                      %msub
                        %mi Y
                        %mi s
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} f_s \colon X_s \to Y_s
                of the underlying
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/sets"} sets
                such that for every
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/open+subset"} open subset
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi A
                      %mo ⊂
                      %msub
                        %mi Y
                        %mi s
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} A \subset Y_s
                and every
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/smooth+function"} smooth function
                of the form
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi ϕ
                      %mo{:lspace => "verythinmathspace"} :
                      %msup
                        %mi ℝ
                        %mi n
                      %mo →
                      %mi X
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \phi \colon \mathbb{R}^n \to X
                the
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/preimage"} preimage
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                      %msub
                        %mi f
                        %mi s
                      %mo ∘
                      %msub
                        %mi ϕ
                        %mi s
                      %msup
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                        %mrow
                          %mo{:lspace => "verythinmathspace", :rspace => "0em"} −
                          %mn 1
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                      %mi A
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                      %mo ⊂
                      %msup
                        %mi ℝ
                        %mi n
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} (f_s \circ \phi_s)^{-1}(A) \subset \mathbb{R}^n
                is open. But this means equivalently that for every such
                = succeed "," do
                  %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                    %semantics
                      %mrow
                        %mi ϕ
                      %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \phi
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi f
                      %mo ∘
                      %mi ϕ
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} f \circ \phi
                is
                = succeed "." do
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/continuous+function"} continuous
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %msub
                        %mi f
                        %mi s
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} f_s
                constitutes a
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/smooth+function"} smooth function
                = succeed "." do
                  %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                    %semantics
                      %mrow
                        %mover
                          %mi f
                          %mo ˜
                        %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                        %mo{:lspace => "verythinmathspace"} :
                        %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                        %mi X
                        %mo ⟶
                        %mi Cdfflg
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                        %mi Y
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                      %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \widetilde f \;\colon\; X \longrightarrow Cdfflg(Y)
              %p
                In summary, we thus have a
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/bijection"} bijection
                of
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/hom-sets"} hom-sets
              .maruku-equation
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mrow
                        %mtable
                          %mtr
                            %mtd
                              %mi Hom
                              %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                              %mi Dtplg
                              %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                              %mi X
                              %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                              %mo ,
                              %mi Y
                              %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                            %mtd
                              %mo ≃
                            %mtd
                              %mi Hom
                              %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                              %mi X
                              %mo ,
                              %mi Cdfflg
                              %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                              %mi Y
                              %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                              %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                          %mtr
                            %mtd
                              %msub
                                %mi f
                                %mi s
                            %mtd
                              %mo ↦
                            %mtd
                              %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                              %mover
                                %mi f
                                %mo ˜
                              %msub
                                %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                                %mi s
                              %mo =
                              %msub
                                %mi f
                                %mi s
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                      \\array{
                      Hom( Dtplg(X), Y )
                      \&amp;\simeq&amp;
                      Hom(X, Cdfflg(Y))
                      \\\
                      f_s &amp;\mapsto&amp; (\widetilde f)_s = f_s
                      }
              %p
                given simply as the
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/identity+function"} identity
                on the underlying
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/functions"} functions
                of underlying sets. This makes it immediate that this hom-isomorphism is
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/natural+bijection"} natural
                in
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi X
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} X
                and
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi Y
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} Y
                and this establishes the
                = succeed "." do
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/adjunction"} adjunction
              %p
                Next, to see that the
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/D-topological+spaces"} D-topological spaces
                are the
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/fixed+point+of+an+adjunction"} fixed points
                of this adjunction, we apply the above
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/natural+bijection"} natural bijection
                on hom-sets to the case
              .maruku-equation
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mrow
                        %mtable
                          %mtr
                            %mtd
                              %mi Hom
                              %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                              %mi Dtplg
                              %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                              %mi Cdfflg
                              %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                              %mi Z
                              %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                              %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                              %mo ,
                              %mi Y
                              %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                            %mtd
                              %mo ≃
                            %mtd
                              %mi Hom
                              %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                              %mi Cdfflg
                              %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                              %mi Z
                              %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                              %mo ,
                              %mi Cdfflg
                              %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                              %mi Y
                              %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                              %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                          %mtr
                            %mtd
                              %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                              %msub
                                %mi ϵ
                                %mi Z
                              %msub
                                %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                                %mi s
                            %mtd
                              %mo ↦
                            %mtd
                              %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                              %mi{:mathvariant => "normal"} id
                              %msub
                                %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                                %mi s
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                      \\array{
                      Hom( Dtplg(Cdfflg(Z)), Y )
                      \&amp;\simeq&amp;
                      Hom(Cdfflg(Z), Cdfflg(Y))
                      \\\
                      (\epsilon_Z)_s &amp;\mapsto&amp; (\mathrm{id})_s
                      }
              %p
                to find that the
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/counit+of+the+adjunction"} counit of the adjunction
              .maruku-equation
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi Dtplg
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                      %mi Cdfflg
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                      %mi X
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                      %mover
                        %mo ⟶
                        %mrow
                          %msub
                            %mi ϵ
                            %mi X
                      %mi X
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                      Dtplg(Cdfflg(X))
                      \\overset{\epsilon_X}{\longrightarrow}
                      X
              %p
                is given by the
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/identity+function"} identity function
                on the underlying sets
                = succeed "." do
                  %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                    %semantics
                      %mrow
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                        %msub
                          %mi ϵ
                          %mi X
                        %msub
                          %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                          %mi s
                        %mo =
                        %msub
                          %mi id
                          %mrow
                            %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                            %msub
                              %mi X
                              %mi s
                            %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                      %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} (\epsilon_X)_s = id_{(X_s)}
              %p
                Therefore
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %msub
                        %mi η
                        %mi X
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \eta_X
                is an
                = succeed "," do
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/isomorphism"} isomorphism
                = succeed "," do
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/homeomorphism"} homeomorphism
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %msub
                        %mi X
                        %mi s
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} X_s
                with respect to the topology on
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi X
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} X
                are precisely those with respect to the topology on
                = succeed "," do
                  %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                    %semantics
                      %mrow
                        %mi Dtplg
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                        %mi Cdfflg
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                        %mi X
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                      %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} Dtplg(Cdfflg(X))
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi X
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} X
                coincide with those whose pre-images under all continuous functions
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi ϕ
                      %mo{:lspace => "verythinmathspace"} :
                      %msup
                        %mi ℝ
                        %mi n
                      %mo →
                      %mi X
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \phi \colon \mathbb{R}^n \to X
                are open. This means equivalently that
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi X
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} X
                is a D-topological space.
              %p
                Finally, to see that we have an
                = succeed "," do
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/idempotent+adjunction"} idempotent adjunction
                = succeed ")" do
                  %a{:href => "idempotent+adjunction#EquivalentConditionsForIdempotency"} this Prop.
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/comonad"} comonad
              .maruku-equation
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi Dtplg
                      %mo ∘
                      %mi Cdfflg
                      %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                      %mo{:lspace => "verythinmathspace"} :
                      %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                      %mi TopologicalSpaces
                      %mo →
                      %mi TopologicalSpaces
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                      Dtplg \circ Cdfflg \;\colon\; TopologicalSpaces \to TopologicalSpaces
              %p
                is an
                = succeed "," do
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/idempotent+comonad"} idempotent comonad
              .maruku-equation
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi Dtplg
                      %mo ∘
                      %mi Cdfflg
                      %mover
                        %mo ⟶
                        %mrow
                          %mi Dtplg
                          %mo ⋅
                          %mi η
                          %mo ⋅
                          %mi Cdfflg
                      %mi Dtplg
                      %mo ∘
                      %mi Cdfflg
                      %mo ∘
                      %mi Dtplg
                      %mo ∘
                      %mi Cdfflg
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                      Dtplg \circ Cdfflg
                      \\overset{
                      Dtplg \cdot \eta \cdot Cdfflg
                      }{\longrightarrow}
                      Dtplg \circ Cdfflg \circ Dtplg \circ Cdfflg
              %p
                is a
                = succeed "." do
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/natural+isomorphism"} natural isomorphism
                = succeed "," do
                  %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                    %semantics
                      %mrow
                        %mi ϵ
                      %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \epsilon
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/adjunction+unit"} adjunction unit
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi η
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \eta
                is the
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/identity+function"} identity function
                on the underlying sets. Therefore, this being a natural isomorphism is equivalent to the operation of passing to the D-topological refinement of the topology of a topological space being an idempotent operation, which is clearly the case.
          %h2#References References
          %p A proof of a model structure on diffeological spaces, with weak equivalences detected on standard smooth homotopy groups, is claimed in
          %ul
            %li#HaraguchiShimakawa13
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Tadayuki+Haraguchi"}> Tadayuki Haraguchi
              ,
              = succeed "," do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Kazuhisa+Shimakawa"} Kazuhisa Shimakawa
              %em A model structure on the category of diffeological spaces
              (
              %a{:href => "https://arxiv.org/abs/1311.5668"}> arXiv:1311.5668
              )
          %p
            though
            %a{:href => "#Kihara16"} Kihara 16
            writes (
            %a{:href => "https://arxiv.org/pdf/1605.06794.pdf#page=2"}> p. 2
            ) that
          %blockquote
            %p
              there exists a gap in the proof of
              = succeed "," do
                %a{:href => "#HaraguchiShimakawa13"} Haraguchi-Shimakawa 13
          %p This gap has been filled in
          %ul
            %li#Haraguchi18
              %p
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Tadayuki+Haraguchi"}> Tadayuki Haraguchi
                ,
                %em Homotopy structures of smooth CW complexes
                (
                %a{:href => "https://arxiv.org/abs/1811.06175"}> arXiv:1811.06175
                )
            %li#HaraguchiShimakawa20
              %p
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Tadayuki+Haraguchi"}> Tadayuki Haraguchi
                ,
                = succeed "," do
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Kazuhisa+Shimakawa"} Kazuhisa Shimakawa
                = succeed "," do
                  %em A model structure on the category of diffeological spaces, I
                = succeed "&rbrack;" do
                  %a{:href => "https://arxiv.org/abs/2011.12842"} arXiv:2011.12842
          %p A different model structure, however not using the standard smooth homotopy groups(!), is claimed (and published) in
          %ul
            %li#Kihara16
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Hiroshi+Kihara"}> Hiroshi Kihara
              ,
              = succeed "," do
                %em Model category of diffeological spaces
              = succeed ")" do
                %a{:href => "https://arxiv.org/abs/1605.06794"} arXiv:1605.06794
          %p See also
          %ul
            %li#ChristensenWu14
              %p
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/J.+Daniel+Christensen"}> J. Daniel Christensen
                ,
                = succeed "," do
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Enxin+Wu"} Enxin Wu
                = succeed "," do
                  %em The homotopy theory of diffeological spaces, I. Fibrant and cofibrant objects
                = succeed ")" do
                  %a{:href => "http://arxiv.org/abs/1311.6394"} arXiv:1311.6394
            %li
              %p
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Hiroshi+Kihara"}> Hiroshi Kihara
                ,
                %em Quillen equivalences between the model categories of smooth spaces, simplicial sets, and arc-gengerated spaces
                (
                %a{:href => "https://arxiv.org/abs/1702.04070"}> arXiv:1702.04070
                )
            %li
              %p
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Tadayuki+Haraguchi"}> Tadayuki Haraguchi
                ,
                = succeed "," do
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Kazuhisa+Shimakawa"} Kazuhisa Shimakawa
                %em On homotopy types of diffeological cell complexes
                (
                %a{:href => "https://arxiv.org/abs/1912.05359"}> arXiv:1912.05359
                )
        .revisedby
